# Files that run with production credentials, or that could weaken the
# release gate, need the repository owner's review (the "main protection"
# ruleset requires Code Owner review). Everything else merges with CI only.
#
# Rule for this file: every file that a job holding a production credential
# executes or reads as configuration must be listed here. The credentialed
# jobs (release.yml `push`, ota-production.yml `upload`, ota-rollback.yml
# `republish`, migrate-production.yml `apply`) are designed to execute no
# repository code and no repository dependencies, so the list is:
#
#   /.github/                - all workflows (they define what the
#                              credentialed jobs do, and what "CI green"
#                              means), the release-gate scripts, the pinned
#                              eas-cli lockfile (.github/ota/eas-cli/), and
#                              this CODEOWNERS file itself.
#   /apps/mobile/app.json    - read by eas-cli in the OTA upload/rollback jobs
#                              (EAS project, owner, update URL, runtime
#                              version policy; the workflows also pin these).
#   /apps/mobile/eas.json    - read by eas-cli in the same jobs (cli settings).
#
# Deliberately not listed:
#   - apps/mobile/package.json: the OTA jobs only extract two validated
#     version strings from it and write their own package.json.
#   - apps/mobile/supabase/migrations/: each run's approval summary shows the
#     exact SQL and its SHA-256, and the apply job refuses any other bytes, so
#     the owner approves the content at the moment it runs.
#   - the OTA bundle's source: it is released code (already on `production`),
#     built in a job with no credentials, and digest-checked after approval.
/.github/ @ZenFinanceHub
/apps/mobile/app.json @ZenFinanceHub
/apps/mobile/eas.json @ZenFinanceHub
